WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.340
YouTube is branching out as a streaming service.

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:07.491
You can rent or purchase films directly through
the site for a small fee, but now, they're

00:00:07.491 --> 00:00:12.310
setting themselves apart from the pack by
releasing almost 100 films for free, well,

00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:13.600
free with ad breaks, at least.

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:16.620
Here are some of the best free movies YouTube
has to offer.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:21.940
2014's Very Good Girls certainly has all the
marks of a prestige indie film.

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:27.060
Its cast includes Demi Moore, Ellen Barkin,
Richard Dreyfuss and Peter Sarsgaard alongside

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.420
stars Dakota Fanning and Elizabeth Olsen.

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:33.630
You may recognize her as the younger sibling
of the Olsen twins, who has since made a name

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:36.790
for herself as Scarlet Witch in the Marvel
Cinematic Universe.

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:41.190
The film tells the story of two young women,
Lily and Gerri, who fall for the same boy,

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:44.780
David, played by Boyd Holbrook, during their
last summer before college.

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:49.480
Both girls have to weather personal strife
that goes beyond typical teenage girl drama,

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:53.480
complicated by the fact that David is more
interested in Lily, creating a rift between

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:54.200
the two friends.

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:58.760
The film wasn't exactly a hit with critics,
but it was praised for its sharp writing and

00:00:58.760 --> 00:00:59.940
excellent performances.

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:03.800
If you haven't heard of it, it's worth a watch,
and anyone who struggled through their teenage

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:08.580
years will absolutely find a moment or two
that are incredibly, sometimes painfully relatable.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:15.600
This 2011 documentary by director David Gelb
focuses on Jiro Ono, an 85-year-old master

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:20.579
chef and the proprietor of Sukiyabashi Jiro,
an extremely unique Michelin-starred sushi

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:21.660
restaurant in Tokyo.

00:01:22.009 --> 00:01:27.780
The legendary restaurant only offers a 20-course
fixed menu of dishes that cost at least 30,000

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:30.880
Japanese yen, or just under 300 US dollars.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:36.179
The restaurant also has only ten seats, and
is located, oddly enough, inside of a subway

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:36.680
station.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:41.200
The movie also shines a light on Ono's children,
who each follow their father's footsteps in

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:41.940
their own ways.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:46.240
Takashi, Jiro's younger son, left the nest
to open a restaurant of his own elsewhere

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:46.880
in Japan.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:52.140
His older brother, Yoshikazu, considers himself
duty-bound to take over Sukiyabashi Jiro one

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:54.720
day, and is shown still working alongside
their father.

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:59.100
Originally, Gelb was going to make a documentary
about sushi culture in general, but after

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:03.709
eating at Jiro's restaurant, he was struck
by the chef's artistry, commitment, and focus,

00:02:03.709 --> 00:02:05.380
not to mention his incredible sushi.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:08.360
He then decided to focus exclusively on Jiro
instead.

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:11.300
You don't need to be a foodie to enjoy the
movie, either.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:14.080
The film has been met with near-universal
critical acclaim.

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:18.920
It was even parodied by Fred Armisen on his
series Documentary Now, on which Armisen learns

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:22.520
how to make the perfect grain of rice from
his father, a no-nonsense chef.

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:27.340
Some have described Jiro Dreams of Sushi as
a perfect antidote to today's haphazard and

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:31.810
hectic culture, in that watching a master
of his craft perfect his techniques through

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:36.180
constant, patient practice may inspire viewers
to stop chasing the next big thing and learn

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:36.760
to focus.

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:42.540
The late, great Stan Lee was more than just
a comic book writer, he was a self-made superhero

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:44.040
and a legend unto himself.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:49.360
After his passing at the age of 95 in 2018,
there's no better time to watch With Great

00:02:49.379 --> 00:02:53.590
Power: The Stan Lee Story, which chronicles
everything from his childhood to the creation

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:56.680
of seminal characters like the Hulk, Spider-Man,
and the X-Men.

00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:00.860
Lee's life was so long and storied that many
may have forgotten how many things he lived

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:01.980
through and accomplished.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:04.420
As a younger man, he served in World War II.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:09.440
When he returned home and got into the comics
industry in the 1950s, he engaged in a hard-fought

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:11.700
battle to prevent comic books from being censored.

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:16.790
The documentary wisely lets Lee speak for
himself through most of its 80-minute runtime,

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:18.500
telling stories about his humble beginnings.

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:23.600
A particularly moving anecdote reveals that
he once came close to quitting comics altogether

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:27.710
until his wife, Joan, convinced him to write
what he really wanted to write about, which

00:03:27.710 --> 00:03:30.260
resulted in the creation of the Fantastic
Four.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:35.000
No documentary on Stan Lee would be complete
without plenty of Marvel stars and celebrities

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:39.459
to talk about his influence, and a wealth
of famous faces appear, from Tobey Maguire

00:03:39.459 --> 00:03:42.480
and Samuel L. Jackson to Paris Hilton and
Ringo Starr.

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:47.450
This film serves as the perfect ode to an
icon and shows that he was still, at his core,

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:52.120
relatable and accessible, even as perhaps
the most influential man in comic book history.

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:57.040
"You know, I guess one person can make a difference."

00:03:57.620 --> 00:04:02.500
An ambitious yet seriously low-budget science
fiction film from Ecuadorian director Sebastián

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:06.280
Cordero, Europa Report features a few actors
you might recognize.

00:04:06.469 --> 00:04:10.920
The movie stars Embeth Davidtz, best known
for Schindler's List and Matilda, as well

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:15.330
as the late Michael Nyqvist, who appeared
in Mission: Impossible - Ghost Protocol, John

00:04:15.330 --> 00:04:17.140
Wick, and the Swedish Millennium series.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:21.700
The movie focuses on a group of astronauts
searching for life on Europa, one of Jupiter's

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:22.200
moons.

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:26.740
Six months into the mission, the ship is suddenly
hit by a solar storm which leaves them unable

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:28.400
to communicate with anyone on Earth.

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:32.930
They then suffer a series of accidents before
eventually landing on Europa, discovering

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:36.000
evidence that a single-celled organism exists
on the planet.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:40.210
Though they manage to restore their communications,
the crew never makes it back to Earth, leaving

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:42.780
behind only a video that gets transmitted
back home.

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:47.520
The making of the film was extremely faithful
to the realities of space travel and of Europa

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:51.970
itself, the filmmakers used maps for accuracy,
and they used footage of space walks from

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:55.800
the International Space Station and space
shuttle to correctly portray how a human might

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:56.880
move within space.

00:04:57.140 --> 00:05:02.380
These tactics paid off when it came to critical
reception, among other positive reviews, space.com

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:06.979
noted that the film was extraordinarily realistic,
and it was nominated for a Bradbury Award

00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:10.580
by the Science Fiction and Fantasy Writers
of America in 2013.

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:16.180
Flawless features an all-star pair as its
two main cast members, Demi Moore and Michael

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:18.780
Caine, both of whom shine in this creative
heist thriller.

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:23.530
The film opens on Laura Quinn, who is being
interviewed for a relatively superficial piece

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:26.400
about being the first woman to run the London
Diamond Corporation.

00:05:26.830 --> 00:05:30.460
But things take a turn when she suddenly places
an enormous diamond on the table in front

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:32.280
of her and announces that she stole it.

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:36.910
In a flashback to 1960, the film tells the
story of Quinn's early days at the London

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:41.460
Diamond Corporation, where she keeps losing
jobs to relatively unqualified men.

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:45.600
Making things worse, she finds out from the
building's janitor, Mr. Hobbs, that she's

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:49.740
not only not going to be promoted, but that
the higher-ups are planning to fire her.

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:53.800
Together, they put together a plan to rob
the Corporation, but as with every good heist

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:57.860
film, several twists and turns keep Quinn
and Hobbs from easily accomplishing their

00:05:57.860 --> 00:05:58.360
goals.

00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:02.620
At every fork in the road, the two are tracked
by Mr. Finch, a private investigator hired

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:04.060
to look into their amateur heist.

00:06:04.389 --> 00:06:08.460
While the film earned lukewarm reviews from
critics at the time of its release, it's still

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:12.600
well worth a watch, featuring an engrossing
story with a number of sharp turns, as well

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:13.840
as an excellent cast.

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:19.220
This Oscar-nominated documentary about the
excesses of one Christian summer camp may

00:06:19.220 --> 00:06:22.880
seem, at first, that it's choosing sides purely
by existing.

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:27.200
But Rachel Grady and Heidi Ewing, the directors
of Jesus Camp, have assured viewers that they

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:29.520
truly had no agenda during the making of their
film.

00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:33.840
According to the filmmakers, they always intended
the movie to simply be an accurate and honest

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:38.669
representation of camps that aim to radicalize
Christian teenagers, indoctrinating them with

00:06:38.669 --> 00:06:41.500
a drive to take back the country in the name
of Jesus Christ.

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:46.680
The film focuses on a camp based in North
Dakota called the Kids of Fire School of Ministry,

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:51.199
turning an even narrower focus to three children
who attend, Levi, Rachael, and Tory.

00:06:51.199 --> 00:06:55.230
Switching between the camp itself and a prayer
conference in Missouri at Christ Triumphant

00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:58.919
Church, the film casts the camp's leader,
Becky Fischer, in a dubious light.

00:06:58.919 --> 00:07:03.000
The movie includes tense scenes such as an
encounter between Fischer and conservative

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:08.389
talk radio host Mike Papantonio, who questions
the camp leader's choice to push extreme messages

00:07:08.389 --> 00:07:09.280
on young children.

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:13.460
The film immediately stirred up controversy
by showing scenes where children were seemingly

00:07:13.460 --> 00:07:18.199
indoctrinated against, quote, "Muslim extremists,"
and told to become members of a so-called

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.140
"army of God."

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:24.460
Many critics viewed the portrayal of evangelical
Christians as unflinching and sometimes disturbing,

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:27.920
and Fischer eventually shut down the camp
amidst criticism of her teaching methods.

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:32.000
She also cited concerns about vandalism in
the aftermath of the film when she closed

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:32.500
the camp.

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:37.000
Whenever a documentary incites that kind of
intense reaction, it's usually worth a watch.

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:42.700
Based on actual events, The World's Fastest
Indian tells the story of Burt Munro, a real-life

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:47.380
speed racer from Invercargill, New Zealand
who famously rode an Indian Scout motorcycle

00:07:47.380 --> 00:07:49.240
that he outfitted to his own specifications.

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:54.439
Munro, as played by Anthony Hopkins, set a
high number of land speed records for motorcycles

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:58.820
with engines under 1,000cc throughout the
1950s and 1960s.

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:03.380
As the film tells us, he encountered a number
of hardships on this path to speed and glory.

00:08:03.380 --> 00:08:07.880
After irritating his neighbors at home in
New Zealand, he hops a cargo ship to the States.

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:12.380
While he's initially looked down upon by the
people of Los Angeles, he eventually succeeds

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:14.920
thanks to a can-do attitude and pure friendliness.

00:08:14.980 --> 00:08:19.940
Overcoming the odds, he arrives at the Bonneville
Salt Flats, the real-life home of the Bonneville

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:24.060
Speedway, and ends up breaking several records
before returning home to New Zealand as a

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:24.560
hero.

00:08:24.660 --> 00:08:28.600
Though some criticized the movie for being
historically inaccurate, the film received

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:30.720
praise from both audiences and critics.

00:08:31.380 --> 00:08:35.900
Infamous outlaw Butch Cassidy and his accomplice,
the Sundance Kid, have been profiled almost

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:37.580
countless times in pop culture.

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:41.720
One interpretation of the story is the movie
Blackthorn, starring lauded playwright and

00:08:41.729 --> 00:08:46.540
actor Sam Shepard as an aged Cassidy, hiding
out in South America under the name James

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:47.040
Blackthorn.

00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:51.980
Shepard is joined by Nikolai-Coster Waldau
as a young Cassidy, who you may recognize

00:08:51.980 --> 00:08:54.230
as Jaime Lannister from Game of Thrones.

00:08:54.230 --> 00:08:58.630
The film follows Butch returning to the United
States after the death of another Wild Bunch

00:08:58.630 --> 00:08:59.880
accomplice, Etta Price.

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:04.560
Along the way, he is attacked by a mysterious
Spaniard, and the two eventually team up for

00:09:04.579 --> 00:09:08.430
a robbery, leading to plenty of betrayals
and backstabbing along the way.

00:09:08.430 --> 00:09:12.660
The film received mixed reviews from critics,
undoubtedly suffering from comparisons to

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:14.560
other depictions of Butch Cassidy in film.

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:18.720
Critics wrote that while some parts of the
film worked splendidly, it fell victim to

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:20.260
certain Western cliches.

00:09:20.300 --> 00:09:24.220
But while the film as a whole has some flaws,
Shepard's performance was singled out for

00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:28.380
praise in a wide array of reviews, making
something special out of this character study

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:29.510
of a legendary outlaw.

00:09:30.510 --> 00:09:34.640
A small independent film that made a fairly
big impression, Great World of Sound came

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:39.680
out during the height of the reality TV phenomenon
in the late 2000s, when it seemed like anybody

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:43.579
could become instantly famous, so long as
they had a little bit of skill and a whole

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:44.100
lot of luck.

00:09:44.420 --> 00:09:50.340
Directed by Craig Zobel, this unorthodox pseudo-documentary
features Pat Healy as Martin and Kene Holliday

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:55.120
as Clarence, two men undercover on an actual
audition circuit who convince strangers to

00:09:55.120 --> 00:09:59.200
perform for them in exchange for free recording
sessions and industry contacts.

00:09:59.420 --> 00:10:03.480
The people auditioning, tricked into thinking
the two actors were record industry executives,

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:08.610
were for the most part entirely unaware that
the project was a film shoot, exposing themselves

00:10:08.610 --> 00:10:10.360
fully to the faux-documentarians.

00:10:10.690 --> 00:10:14.800
With a fictional throughline running alongside
real-life audition footage, the movie ultimately

00:10:14.810 --> 00:10:19.290
blurs fact and fiction, ending up being an
incredibly revealing look at the desire some

00:10:19.290 --> 00:10:20.560
have for fame and celebrity.

00:10:21.110 --> 00:10:25.660
Despite being hard to categorize, Great World
of Sound was well-received by critics.

00:10:25.660 --> 00:10:30.750
In his positive, three-star review, Roger
Ebert said the film was confident and well-designed,

00:10:30.750 --> 00:10:32.990
defying genre to make a memorable viewing
experience.

